{
 "slug": "test/measurement-complete",
 "about": "Every path that completes a measurement, and every one that clears it, and the loaded-settings warning those paths move. Each case starts a fresh analyzer (Classical Guitar, 1 tap, threshold −40, warm-up passed) and runs its 'steps' in order: {\"numberOfTaps\": n} sets the tap count before anything is captured; {\"captureTaps\": [dB, …]} holds one captured tap per entry — 64 bins at 31.25 Hz, −80 dB but bin 16 at that level; {\"processTaps\": true} processes the captured taps as the end of a capture does; {\"newTap\": true} starts a new sequence; {\"cancel\": true} cancels; {\"load\": file} loads that inline file; {\"warning\": true} raises the loaded-settings warning; {\"setTaps\": n} changes Taps as the user does; {\"setThreshold\": dB} changes the threshold as the user does. 'expect' after the last step: 'complete', 'frozenSpectrum' (a frozen spectrum is held), 'detecting', 'loadedSettingsWarning', 'numberOfTaps'. Expected values are Swift's.",
